// spec ch05 §5.12 / book ch11-01: a by-value capture becomes an owned
// field holding a copy of the referent, so capturing a reference-typed
// local by value is legal and creates no borrow of the referent -- the
// closure carries no lifetime dependency on `r` or on `x`.
int main() {
    int x = 7;
    int& r = x;
    auto i = [r]() { return r; };
    return i();
}
